[{:db/id "q-332860/field-1/e31d31ecaec1af779ab200651c6a0f07e21dfb1f2ae879e08de5b2c2d4c126c6" :answer/id #uuid "28042130-a426-5365-b3ae-cd7ffc0d0c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{17}\\cos(x)-\\frac{20}{17}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332860/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "60ab66f8-e8e7-5656-acd4-0e211d62b79b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332860/field-1/e31d31ecaec1af779ab200651c6a0f07e21dfb1f2ae879e08de5b2c2d4c126c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-332860/field-1/e31d31ecaec1af779ab200651c6a0f07e21dfb1f2ae879e08de5b2c2d4c126c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332860" :question/id #uuid "568328bb-23be-5be3-8f34-0286313daa0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332860" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(\\beta -4\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha -4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta -4\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha -4\\beta =5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{5}{17},$ $\\beta =-\\frac{20}{17}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{5}{17}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\frac{20}{17}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332860/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332860"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332754/field-1/68402d56776c0a28f26e5426111a0a44f897e94384e682a072acc09001ef87a0" :answer/id #uuid "ee80fd5c-1152-52d7-9040-18d54ad7e497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(x)-\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332754/field-1/d2c052f5e7b61b387aefc25f0b37b36cb05a1c27f8aed84a13e1f32e35d1e38a" :answer/id #uuid "b7d4c1e8-6e35-55ec-9561-28c79fb83134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(x)+\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332754/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc2444ce-4d51-5445-ae10-b762660dbb17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332754/field-1/68402d56776c0a28f26e5426111a0a44f897e94384e682a072acc09001ef87a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-332754/field-1/68402d56776c0a28f26e5426111a0a44f897e94384e682a072acc09001ef87a0" "q-332754/field-1/d2c052f5e7b61b387aefc25f0b37b36cb05a1c27f8aed84a13e1f32e35d1e38a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332754" :question/id #uuid "3e284231-5833-58cc-bb3d-307106a8a4f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-332754" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(4\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha +\\beta =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha +4\\beta =-5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $\\beta =3-4\\alpha .$ Substituting into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n-\\alpha +4(3-4\\alpha )=-5\\,⇒\\,\\alpha =1.\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\beta =3-4\\alpha =3-4(1)=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332754/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332677/field-1/721c2447ab172a9cb358dcaf728d116fabc79445b06a342d4238fb4e3eb97cad" :answer/id #uuid "96a74151-a29f-5b61-916a-88ecc55baaae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{13}\\cos(x)+\\frac{5}{13}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332677/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e9ccac3-e70f-52ef-a50b-febd8ed4a48a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332677/field-1/721c2447ab172a9cb358dcaf728d116fabc79445b06a342d4238fb4e3eb97cad" :answer-field/choices ["q-332677/field-1/721c2447ab172a9cb358dcaf728d116fabc79445b06a342d4238fb4e3eb97cad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332677" :question/id #uuid "d04aa2bf-f2cb-5499-8059-df387b70eb04" :question/math-academy-id "q-332677" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-5x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+5(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(5\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha +5\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5\\alpha +\\beta =10\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha +5\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{25}{13},\\beta =\\frac{5}{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{25}{13}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\frac{5}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332677/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332869/field-1/56aea7a74cbe9fd97f8897f6e480b9307339b020384692b36e7572d53e7e9a95" :answer/id #uuid "a5259930-07ee-5f4f-8343-f4122d0fe55d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{13}\\cos(x)-\\frac{2}{13}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332869/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823" :answer/id #uuid "4a24a08b-1a10-507e-8d3a-a43c79dadb40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332869/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "37ca03af-e9de-50a2-b5b5-4c4947555481" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332869/field-1/56aea7a74cbe9fd97f8897f6e480b9307339b020384692b36e7572d53e7e9a95" :answer-field/choices ["q-332869/field-1/56aea7a74cbe9fd97f8897f6e480b9307339b020384692b36e7572d53e7e9a95" "q-332869/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332869" :question/id #uuid "4e46092f-0a05-5c5a-96e0-3314344c4d0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-332869" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-5(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(\\beta -5\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha -5\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta -5\\alpha =-4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha -5\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{10}{13},$ $\\beta =-\\frac{2}{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{10}{13}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\frac{2}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332869/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332869"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332676/field-1/99ee2afba3030f1894a53f9688768334744895dc6abbfab5ee13223b10fd7e34" :answer/id #uuid "1aef0022-2654-5a25-bb46-6ae9362d7b33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}\\cos(x)+\\frac{4}{5}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332676/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9566028-7471-501e-bd7f-492ba6563068" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332676/field-1/99ee2afba3030f1894a53f9688768334744895dc6abbfab5ee13223b10fd7e34" :answer-field/choices ["q-332676/field-1/99ee2afba3030f1894a53f9688768334744895dc6abbfab5ee13223b10fd7e34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332676" :question/id #uuid "2145790b-68f6-55bf-951c-b255f46040c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-332676" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+3(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(3\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha +3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\alpha +\\beta =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha +3\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{12}{5},\\beta =\\frac{4}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{12}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332676/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332446/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "c14767b0-cb7d-577d-be4c-6593c6b0262a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228018 :answer-field/correct "q-332446/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-332446/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332446/field-2/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "17b16738-a29d-525a-9ec8-911c0cdb5ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228019 :answer-field/correct "q-332446/field-2/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-332446/field-2/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-332446"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{2x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n3\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n3(-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))-6(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(-6\\alpha +6\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-6\\alpha -6\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6\\alpha +6\\beta =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ -6\\alpha -6\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{3},\\beta =\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+(-\\frac{1}{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(\\frac{1}{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845/field-1/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "4095baf9-b4de-5f6b-af71-3dd60f8b7309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8461ca67-4934-52ca-a221-0e7bb6beeec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa6267a9-2559-503a-b1da-b3327fb0fb87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332845/field-1/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-332845/field-1/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-332845/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845/field-2/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer/id #uuid "60226fd6-bed1-5be2-a8f5-2cf86e9104fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb2df0a-de0c-5c25-959d-75517e2353fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332845/field-2/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer-field/choices ["q-332845/field-2/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332845" :question/id #uuid "9fab2fcc-67fc-5d93-ae27-acd72bba8f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332845" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+14y=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{-2x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n7\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+14{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n7(-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))+14(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(14\\alpha +14\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-14\\alpha +14\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}14\\alpha +14\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ -14\\alpha +14\\beta =-4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{7},\\beta =-\\frac{1}{7}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+(\\frac{1}{7})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-\\frac{1}{7})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332845/field-1" "q-332845/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7a2bbc-4172-591e-98eb-f7586d3ae06b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332894/field-1/61ae9ee7f3aca674ad3b1fe17900a46cbc8790772ac7db4f5c49c425ae7a37bb" :answer/id #uuid "8dcc05fb-c728-5fff-aadd-15c11b2546b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332894/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d6b6577-549f-5d31-a27c-91278d46493c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332894/field-1/61ae9ee7f3aca674ad3b1fe17900a46cbc8790772ac7db4f5c49c425ae7a37bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-332894/field-1/61ae9ee7f3aca674ad3b1fe17900a46cbc8790772ac7db4f5c49c425ae7a37bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332894/field-2/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "527e10a1-d6c5-5426-89cc-8bc07d738d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332894/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1476aebf-f8a6-5f0b-b07e-d140f856fa4f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332894/field-2/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer-field/choices ["q-332894/field-2/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332894" :question/id #uuid "a5973026-0586-52f6-a05b-32d828c1cbc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-332894" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{-3x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+12{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+12(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(12\\beta +12\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-12\\alpha +12\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}12\\alpha +12\\beta =-8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -12\\alpha +12\\beta =11\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{19}{24},\\beta =\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{19}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+(-\\frac{19}{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(\\frac{1}{8})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332894/field-1" "q-332894/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7a2bbc-4172-591e-98eb-f7586d3ae06b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332778/field-1/16dbe5d6761bf7d88e2e94e53900f8b04633401a343287541dbdc88d8b59fedb" :answer/id #uuid "1fd72fd2-6aa2-5947-a27e-c23dcd377d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332778/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ee1356d6-fdec-569c-b07a-e13efdb2214f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332778/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bccf3204-9017-5355-9b45-bb8b6f0e49ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332778/field-1/16dbe5d6761bf7d88e2e94e53900f8b04633401a343287541dbdc88d8b59fedb" :answer-field/choices ["q-332778/field-1/16dbe5d6761bf7d88e2e94e53900f8b04633401a343287541dbdc88d8b59fedb" "q-332778/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b05